  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will build \neastward across Northern Nevada this afternoon into Monday. As a \nresult, a warming trend is expected today and Monday. By Monday\nafternoon, high temperatures will be near normal for this time of\nyear. A trough of low pressure will move eastward across Northern\nNevada Monday afternoon and Monday evening, resulting in a slight\nchance of valley rain and mountain snow. Any precipitation \nassociated with this atmospheric disturbance will remain north of \nInterstate 80. Precipitation chances will be highest near the \nNevada/Idaho border. Precipitation amounts will be no higher than\none tenth of an inch.\n\nZonal flow aloft is anticipated Tuesday through Thursday. This\nwill result in dry weather and temperatures slightly below\nseasonal values. An Eastern Pacific storm system may begin to\nimpact Northern and Central Nevada as early as Friday morning.\nPrecipitation chances will increase Friday afternoon through\nSaturday as this storm system moves closer to the west coast of\nthe United States. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding a warming trend today and Monday. Low forecast \nconfidence in the possibility of valley rain and mountain snow in  \nNorthern Nevada Monday afternoon and Monday evening. Moderate\nforecast confidence regarding dry and relatively cool conditions\nTuesday through Thursday. Moderate forecast confidence in\nincreasing precipitation chances Friday and Saturday. No\ndeviations from the NBM model output.",
